				"id": "ch30",
				"part": "7",
				"title": "Digital FM Receivers and RDS Data",
				"html": "<p class=\"lede\">Building and using digital FM receivers is a must for any zombie survivor. Learn how to decode station data, from the call sign to the song playing, even when the zombies are tuning in. We’ll walk you through the hardware and software needed to build your own receiver, and show you how to use RDS data to stay informed and entertained.</p>\n<h2>The Basics of Digital FM Reception</h2>\n<p>Digital FM receivers use a variety of technologies to decode station data. From the call sign to the song playing, RDS data keeps you informed and entertained. In a zombie apocalypse, a digital FM receiver is your lifeline to the outside world.</p>\n<h2>Building Your Own Digital FM Receiver</h2>\n<p>You don’t need a fancy receiver to get started. With a few scavenged parts, you can build your own digital FM receiver. Start with an FM receiver module, which can be found in old radios, TVs, or even car stereos. Pair it with a microcontroller, and you’ve got the brains of your receiver. Add a display for feedback, and you’re ready to roll.</p>\n<h2>The Protocols of Apocalypse FM</h2>\n<p>Digital FM receivers use a variety of protocols, including RDS and RBDS. These standards ensure that your receiver can decode station data from any broadcaster, no matter who built it. In a zombie apocalypse, interoperability is key. You never know what kind of tech you’ll find in a scavenged receiver, so stick to the standards.</p>\n<h2>Security in the Apocalypse</h2>\n<p>Security is a major concern when the world is falling apart. Digital FM receivers use encryption and authentication to protect your data. In a zombie apocalypse, you’ll want to use the strongest encryption available. Look for systems that support AES-128 or higher, and always keep your software up to date. If you’re building your own system, make sure to implement secure key management and regular firmware updates.</p>\n<h2>The Future of Apocalypse FM</h2>\n<p>As the world rebuilds, digital FM receivers will become even more important. With the rise of digital broadcasting and decentralized communication, you might find yourself building your own receiver from scratch. Whether you’re using RDS, RBDS, or something entirely new, the future of apocalypse FM is bright.</p>",
