				"title": "WiFi and SHF Radar for Zombie Detection",
				"html": "<p class=\"lede\">WiFi and SHF radar are your eyes and ears in a zombie apocalypse. Learn how to use these technologies to detect movement and track zombies, with practical build guides and real-world examples. We’ll cover the hardware and software needed to build your own WiFi and SHF radar systems, and show you how to use them to stay one step ahead of the undead.</p>\n<h2>The Basics of WiFi and SHF Radar</h2>\n<p>WiFi and SHF radar use a variety of technologies to detect movement and track zombies. From simple motion detection to advanced tracking, these systems keep you safe and informed. In a zombie apocalypse, WiFi and SHF radar are your lifeline to the outside world.</p>\n<h2>Building Your Own WiFi and SHF Radar System</h2>\n<p>You don’t need a fancy system to get started. With a few scavenged parts, you can build your own WiFi and SHF radar system. Start with a WiFi module, which can be found in old routers, laptops, or even smartphones. Pair it with a microcontroller, and you’ve got the brains of your system. Add a display for feedback, and you’re ready to roll.</p>\n<h2>The Protocols of Apocalypse WiFi and SHF Radar</h2>\n<p>WiFi and SHF radar use a variety of protocols, including 802.11 and 24 GHz radar. These standards ensure that your system can detect movement from any broadcaster, no matter who built it. In a zombie apocalypse, interoperability is key. You never know what kind of tech you’ll find in a scavenged system, so stick to the standards.</p>\n<h2>Security in the Apocalypse</h2>\n<p>Security is a major concern when the world is falling apart. WiFi and SHF radar use encryption and authentication to protect your data. In a zombie apocalypse, you’ll want to use the strongest encryption available. Look for systems that support AES-128 or higher, and always keep your software up to date. If you’re building your own system, make sure to implement secure key management and regular firmware updates.</p>\n<h2>The Future of Apocalypse WiFi and SHF Radar</h2>\n<p>As the world rebuilds, WiFi and SHF radar will become even more important. With the rise of digital broadcasting and decentralized communication, you might find yourself building your own system from scratch. Whether you’re using 802.11, 24 GHz radar, or something entirely new, the future of apocalypse WiFi and SHF radar is bright.</p>",
